#. engine/messages/plot.py (ticket 18): why a page of a Discipline's PDF matched no sheet. The first is m0-screens 6.13's "No Plot, and why", verbatim. {page} counts from 1.
msgid "engine.plot.names_no_sheet"
msgstr "PDF page {page} could not be matched: neither its title block nor the text on the page names a sheet."

#. The page names two or more sheets' numbers, none more clearly than the others (or one number that two sheets carry, on paper of the same size).
msgid "engine.plot.names_several_sheets"
msgstr "PDF page {page} could not be matched: the text on the page names more than one sheet, and none more clearly than the others."

#. The page has no text at all, only lines: its lettering was plotted as lines.
msgid "engine.plot.no_text"
msgstr "PDF page {page} could not be matched: it has no text, only lines, so nothing on it names a sheet."

#. The page is a scan (12's rule): a picture, with no text or lines.
msgid "engine.plot.scan"
msgstr "PDF page {page} could not be matched: it is a scanned picture, with no text or lines to read."
